  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi></math> are in arithmetic progression with common difference <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo></math> and the determinant of the matrix <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mtd><mtd><mi>y</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>5</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>k</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>z</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math> is zero, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is"
  },
